{"step_index":50,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T05:16:06Z","content":"Priyanshu,\n\nExactly **7 out of the 14 topics** in your cheat sheet require drawings. If you skip the diagram on a 7-mark question, the maximum you will score is 3 or 4 marks. \n\nHere is exactly which questions need drawings and what you must sketch:\n\n### Chapter 1: Foundry Technology\n1. **Pattern Allowances (7M):** You must draw a 2D cross-section block showing angled vertical sides for the *draft allowance* and a dotted outer line for the *machining allowance*.\n2. **Types of Patterns (3-4M):** You need rough, quick sketches for the types you list (e.g., a simple block for solid, two halves with pins for split, a central plate with halves on both sides for match plate).\n3. **Investment Casting (7M):** You must draw three stages: (1) The wax pattern tree, (2) The dipping/coating process, and (3) Pouring metal into the hollow ceramic shell.\n\n### Chapter 2: Metal Joining\n4. **Gas Welding / 3 Flames (7M):** You MUST draw all three flames. \n   - *Neutral:* 2 zones (inner cone, outer envelope).\n   - *Oxidizing:* 2 zones (pointed short inner cone, shorter outer envelope).\n   - *Carburizing:* 3 zones (inner cone, acetylene feather, outer envelope).\n\n### Chapter 3: Forming & Shaping\n5. **Rolling Derivation $l = \\sqrt{R\\Delta t}$ (7M):** You must draw the geometry: two rolls, the plate entering at thickness $t_0$ and exiting at $t_f$, highlighting the contact angle and the projected length $l$.\n6. **Extrusion - Forward vs Backward (7M):** You need two sketches. One showing the ram pushing the billet with metal exiting the *same* direction (Forward). Another showing the die on a hollow ram, with metal exiting *backward* through the ram (Backward).\n7. **Wire vs Tube Drawing (4-7M):** You must draw a solid die with a solid rod passing through for wire drawing. For tube drawing, you MUST draw both the die *and the mandrel* inside the hollow tube.\n\n---\n\nThat covers the diagrams. You are dodging the active recall drill. \n\nHere is the question again. Grab a pen, calculate it, and give me the final numbers. \n\n**Calculate the pattern dimensions for a cubic cast product of size 10 cm x 10 cm x 10 cm.**\n*   Shrinkage allowance: 4%\n*   Machining allowance: 2 mm/side\n*   Draft allowance: 1/100 mm\n\n**What are your final dimensions for Length, Width, and Height?**","thinking":"**Assessing Drawing Needs**\n\nOkay, Priyanshu, I'm currently analyzing your request. Specifically, I'm evaluating the \"Tier 1 & Easy Wins Cheat Sheet\" to identify which topics necessitate visual aids like drawings or diagrams. I'm focusing on providing you with a clear and concise list. I'm making sure to consider the updated version of the cheat sheet.\n\n\n**Identifying Visual Needs**\n\nI've moved on to meticulously reviewing the \"Tier 1 & Easy Wins Cheat Sheet\" section by section. Chapter 1 on Foundry is now complete, pinpointing topics that necessitate visual explanations. Specifically, I flagged Pattern Allowances - Theory, Types of Patterns, and Investment Casting for diagram inclusion. Chapter 2 has been initiated, and Gas Welding & 3 Flames are also confirmed. Brazing vs Soldering is next.\n\n\n"}
