{"step_index":52,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T07:17:26Z","content":"Priyanshu,\n\nHere are the exact text prompts you can feed into an AI image generator (like ChatGPT, Midjourney, or Claude) to get the textbook-style diagrams you need to draw. I have optimized them for clean, 2D engineering line art.\n\n**1. Pattern Allowances**\n> \"Simple 2D black and white technical line drawing of a foundry pattern cross-section. A square block showing a solid inner line. An outer dotted line surrounding it to indicate 'machining allowance'. The vertical sides of the block have a slight outward taper (angle) indicating 'draft allowance'. Textbook engineering sketch style, white background, clear distinct lines, no shading.\"\n\n**2. Types of Patterns**\n> \"Simple 2D black and white technical line drawing showing three foundry pattern types side-by-side. 1) A split pattern with two halves and alignment dowel pins. 2) A match plate pattern showing a central horizontal plate with pattern halves attached above and below. 3) A gated pattern showing multiple small patterns connected to a central runner. Clean engineering sketch style.\"\n\n**3. Investment Casting**\n> \"Simple 2D black and white technical line drawing showing three stages of investment casting side-by-side. Stage 1: a wax pattern tree. Stage 2: dipping the wax tree into a ceramic slurry tank. Stage 3: pouring liquid metal from a ladle into a hollow ceramic shell. Engineering textbook line art style, flat 2D, no shading.\"\n\n**4. Gas Welding Flames**\n> \"Simple 2D black and white technical line drawing of three oxy-acetylene welding flames side-by-side. Flame 1: Neutral flame with a distinct inner cone and outer envelope. Flame 2: Oxidizing flame with a sharp, short inner cone and short envelope. Flame 3: Carburizing flame showing three distinct zones - an inner cone, an intermediate acetylene feather, and an outer envelope. Engineering sketch.\"\n\n**5. Rolling Derivation Geometry**\n> \"Simple 2D black and white technical diagram of sheet metal rolling geometry. Two large circular rolls rotating in opposite directions. A metal plate passing between them, reducing in thickness from left to right. Show a dashed horizontal centerline, the arc of contact, and a projected horizontal straight line underneath the contact zone to represent the projected length. Textbook schematic style.\"\n\n**6. Forward vs Backward Extrusion**\n> \"Simple 2D black and white technical diagram showing forward and backward extrusion side-by-side. Left (Forward): A solid ram pushing a metal billet to the right through a die, with metal exiting right. Right (Backward): A hollow ram with a die attached pushing left into a billet, with the extruded metal flowing backwards right through the center of the hollow ram. Engineering line art.\"\n\n**7. Wire vs Tube Drawing**\n> \"Simple 2D black and white technical diagram showing wire drawing and tube drawing side-by-side. Left: Wire drawing showing a solid metal rod being pulled through a converging die. Right: Tube drawing showing a hollow tube being pulled through a die, with a fixed internal mandrel (plug) supporting the inner wall of the tube. Engineering textbook schematic, clean lines.\"\n\n---\n\nNow, stop stalling. The mid-sem is testing your ability to calculate, not just draw. \n\n**Calculate the pattern dimensions for a cubic cast product of size 10 cm x 10 cm x 10 cm.**\n*   Shrinkage allowance: 4%\n*   Machining allowance: 2 mm/side\n*   Draft allowance: 1/100 mm\n\n**Give me the final numbers.**","thinking":"**Clarifying the Intent**\n\nOkay, the user's intent is now clear, and I've locked onto the task. The initial request for \"prompt images\" was a bit misleading, and I've parsed the clarification. My focus is now on generating AI image prompts for the 7 questions. I can proceed to consider the best prompt-writing strategy.\n\n\n**Defining Image Prompts**\n\nI'm now generating image prompts based on the seven topics. I've focused on creating detailed specifications for each prompt to guarantee the resulting images meet requirements. I'm focusing on \"textbook style,\" 2D black and white technical sketches. Each one should be simplified line art with labels and no shading. The goal is clarity and precise technical illustration.\n\n\n**Developing Visual Prompts**\n\nI've crafted image prompts that focus on technical clarity, working through the specific details. I'm focusing on \"textbook engineering sketches,\" plain 2D black and white line drawings. For example, for the draft allowance, the image should clearly depict a taper. For pattern types, I'm illustrating split, match plate, and gated patterns, side by side.\n\n\n**Illustrating Key Concepts**\n\nI am now focusing on refining Prompts 5, 6, and 7. Prompt 5, for rolling geometry, will feature a concise diagram of sheet metal rolling. Prompt 6, for extrusion, will show side-by-side forward and backward extrusion diagrams. I'm aiming for clarity in these textbook-style sketches. I am still developing the last prompt.\n\n\n"}
