e":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Predicted additional exam questions beyond Tier 1 and Missing Theory files. Covers all remaining Tier 2, Tier 3, and zero-PYQ syllabus topics with full GTU-format answers. Organized by probability: HIGH (Tier 2), MEDIUM (Tier 3/Borderline), LOW (zero-PYQ but in syllabus).\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"PREDICTED ADDITIONAL EXAM QUESTIONS — BEYOND TIER 1\\n====================================================\\n(Everything NOT already in Tier1_EasyWins_CheatSheet or Missing_Theory_Answers)\\n\\n\\n=====================================================================\\nHIGH PROBABILITY — TIER 2 (Asked 3-4 times in old papers)\\n=====================================================================\\n\\n\\n---------------------------------------------------------\\n1. PROPERTIES OF MOULDING SAND (4-7 Marks)\\nAsked: 3/9 papers\\n---------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nQuestion: Explain the properties of moulding sand.\\n\\nAnswer (Write 6-7 properties for 7M, any 4 for 4M):\\n\\n1. Permeability: The ability of moulding sand to allow gases and steam to pass through it during pouring. If permeability is low, gases get trapped and cause blow holes in the casting.\\n\\n2. Flowability (Plasticity): The ability of sand to flow around the pattern and take the exact shape of the mould cavity. Better flowability = better reproduction of fine details.\\n\\n3. Collapsibility: The ability of the mould to collapse (break down) easily after the casting solidifies. If sand does not collapse, the casting cannot shrink freely and internal stresses or cracks develop.\\n\\n4. Cohesiveness (Strength): The ability of sand grains to stick together. Without cohesiveness, the mould walls will crumble when molten metal is poured.\\n\\n5. Refractoriness: The ability of sand to withstand high temperatures of molten metal without fusing or melting. Silica sand has high refractoriness (~1700 deg C).\\n\\n6. Green Strength: The strength of the mould in its wet (green) condition before drying. Must be enough to hold its shape during handling and core setting.\\n\\n7. Adhesiveness: The ability of sand to stick to the walls of the moulding flask. Without this, the sand falls away from the flask during mould handling.\\n\\n\\n---------------------------------------------------------\\n2. WELDING DEFECTS — CAUSES AND REMEDIES (4-7 Marks)\\nAsked: 3/9 paper\n<truncated 27386 bytes>","Description":"\"All predicted additional exam questions beyond the Tier 1 and Missing Theory files. Covers Tier 2, Tier 3, Borderline, and zero-PYQ syllabus topics with full GTU-format answers.\"","Overwrite":"false","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\cc5ae5f0-3c52-483a-b0d6-e323018f022c\\\\Predicted_Additional_Questions.txt\"","toolAction":"\"Creating predicted questions file\"","toolSummary":"\"Predicted additional exam questions\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
