d defects. I'm noting solutions for slag entrapment, spatter (including current reduction), and various cracks. I'm also including detailed remedies for lack of fusion, which involves increasing heat, correcting electrode angle, and ensuring a clean surface.\n\n\n**Categorizing Welding Techniques**\n\nI am now organizing welding techniques into distinct categories: fusion welding and pressure welding. I'm noting the subdivisions within each, such as gas welding, arc welding, and their variations. I am also classifying allied processes like brazing and soldering. Furthermore, I am noting the importance of a clean tree diagram for GTU examiners.\n\n\n**Describing Core Placement**\n\nI'm now detailing core placement and support mechanisms within the mould. I've categorized core types based on their position: horizontal, vertical, balanced, hanging, and drop cores. My current focus is on clearly defining the core print and its function in creating the necessary seat or recess for core positioning. I'm also describing the purpose and use of chaplets, particularly when core prints are insufficient. I'm noting the need for a metal support that will fuse with the casting. Finally, I'm working on sketching a diagram to visually explain the principles I've noted.\n\n\n**Summarizing the Steps**\n\nI'm now detailing the steps in sand casting. The ordered sequence includes: pattern making, mould preparation, core setting (when applicable), mould closing, pouring molten metal, solidification, shakeout, and finally, cleaning and finishing the casting. I'm focusing on the critical aspects of each step to achieve a comprehensive overview.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Updated Predicted Questions text file. Stripped out medium and low probability topics. Contains only the top 5 high-probability Tier 2 questions (asked 3-4 times in PYQs).\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"PREDICTED ADDITIONAL EXAM QUESTIONS — BEYOND TIER 1\\n====================================================\\n(Only High Probability Tier 2 Topics)\\n\\n=====================================================================\\nHIGH PROBABILITY — TIER 2 (Asked 3-4 times in old papers)\\n=====================================================================\\n\\n---------------------------------------------------------\\n1. PROPERTIES OF MOULDING SAND (4-7 Marks)\\nAsked: 3/9 papers\\n---------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nQuestion: Explain the properties of moulding sand.\\n\\nAnswer (Write 6-7 properties for 7M, any 4 for 4M):\\n\\n1. Permeability: The ability of moulding sand to allow gases and steam to pass through it during pouring. If permeability is low, gases get trapped and cause blow holes in the casting.\\n\\n2. Flowability (Plasticity): The ability of sand to flow around the pattern and take the exact shape of the mould cavity. Better flowability = better reproduction of fine details.\\n\\n3. Collapsibility: The ability of the mould to collapse (break down) easily after the casting solidifies. If sand does not collapse, the casting cannot shrink freely and internal stresses or cracks develop.\\n\\n4. Cohesiveness (Strength): The ability of sand grains to stick together. Without cohesiveness, the mould walls will crumble when molten metal is poured.\\n\\n5. Refractoriness: The ability of sand to withstand high temperatures of molten metal without fusing or melting. Silica sand has high refractoriness (~1700 deg C).\\n\\n6. Green Strength: The strength of the mould in its wet (green) condition before drying. Must be enough to hold its shape during handling and core setting.\\n\\n7. Adhesiveness: The ability of sand to stick to the walls of the moulding flask. Without this, the sand falls away from the flask during mould handling.\\n\\n\\n---------------------------------------------------------\\n2. WELDING DEFECTS — CAUSES AND REMEDIES (4-7 Marks)\\nAsked: 3/9 papers\\n-------------------------------------------\n<truncated 5184 bytes>","Description":"\"Trimmed the file to only include the top 5 high-probability questions. Removed all medium and low probability content.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\cc5ae5f0-3c52-483a-b0d6-e323018f022c\\\\Predicted_Additional_Questions.txt\"","toolAction":"\"Trimming to top 5 questions\"","toolSummary":"\"Truncating text file\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
